Electromagnetism — David Tong (@em-tong: 0, is #reference, #part-of @em-sources) { r_278NEA0Z85RJZSPXQ8G55E3SR1
David Tong, University of Cambridge. [Author's current notes and chapter index](https://davidtong.org/teaching/electromagnetism/) · [Current complete notes](https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/electromagnetism/electro.pdf).

Use the complete author-hosted notes for the advanced undergraduate spine: fields, electrostatics, magnetostatics, electrodynamics, relativity, radiation and electromagnetic matter. Work the associated examples, and distinguish the classical models from their quantum and material limits.

On 29 October 2026 the current file had 236 file pages and retained a Lent Term 2015 title page. This expanded file differs from the older 126-page Part IB PDF at the former Cambridge path and from the commercial textbook. Title and contents were inspected; a page count is not a claim of complete verification. The author supplies free reading; no blanket CC reuse licence is asserted. Link rather than copy text or figures.

